    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1066">

                <pb facs="0788" n="672" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/3746.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Hamm to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Durango</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Federal authorities refuse to allow me to send messages in code to Secretary of
                    State, acting under orders of military headquarters, Torreon. Have also not
                    received any messages from Washington for several days. Hundred twenty Americans
                    in this Consular District as follows: sixty, Torreon; thirty Durango; and thirty
                    scattering. About one half will leave immediately. Please advise if this message
                    received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamm</hi></signed>.</closer>



                <xi:include href="d1066-a1.xml" xpointer="d1066-a1"/>
            </div>
